---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Features — POS Plan';
const description =
  "Everything a small shop needs from a POS: fast billing, barcode scanning, stock tracking, customer dues, installments, multi-outlet support, and daily reports.";
const canonical = 'https://erpboss.com/features';

const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Do I need a barcode scanner to use POS Plan?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'No. You can search products by name, and a barcode scanner speeds up billing if you already have one — no special hardware is required to start.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can I use POS Plan on more than one outlet?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes, POS Plan supports multiple outlets under one shop account, with stock and staff tracked per outlet and stock transfers logged between them.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Do I need to know accounting to use it?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'No. POS Plan is built for shop owners, not accountants — daily sales, stock, and customer dues are shown in plain terms, not ledger entries.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can customers pay in installments?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes. POS Plan supports installment plans for larger purchases, with a dashboard showing what is due today, what is overdue, and a guided way to take a payment against a plan.',
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} jsonLd={[faqJsonLd]}>
  <Nav slot="nav" />

  <h1>Everything a small shop needs. Nothing it doesn't.</h1>
  <p>
    POS Plan focuses on the handful of things a small retailer actually does every day: sell,
    restock, collect what's owed, and keep track of the money. Every feature below ships in the
    same $3/month plan — there's no higher tier hiding the parts you'd actually need.
  </p>

  <h2>Billing</h2>
  <p>
    Search products by name or scan a barcode, add them to the sale, and take cash, card, or a
    partial payment on account. Built for speed during a queue at the counter — the whole flow
    from "customer walks up" to "receipt printed" takes a handful of taps.
  </p>
  <p>
    Returns are handled the same way: pull up the original sale, select what's being returned,
    and stock and the customer's balance are adjusted automatically — no separate spreadsheet to
    reconcile against.
  </p>

  <h2><a href="/inventory">Inventory &amp; stock</a></h2>
  <p>
    Every sale updates stock automatically, and every purchase from a supplier adds to it.
    Track quantity per product, see what's running low before a customer asks for it, and manage
    stock across multiple outlets if you have more than one shop, including transfers between
    locations.
  </p>

  <h2><a href="/barcode">Barcode support</a></h2>
  <p>
    Scan to bill, scan to look up a price, scan to check stock — barcode support is built into
    billing and inventory, not bolted on as an add-on. Works with any standard USB or Bluetooth
    scanner.
  </p>

  <h2><a href="/reports">Daily reports</a></h2>
  <p>
    See today's sales, dues, and cash position without exporting anything. A "Daily Closing"
    step locks each day's numbers, so past sales and payments can't be silently edited once a
    day is closed. Reports are built for a quick end-of-day check, not a finance department.
  </p>

  <h2>Customers, dues &amp; installments</h2>
  <p>
    Keep a simple record of regular customers and what they owe on credit. For larger purchases
    sold on payments over time, POS Plan runs a full installment plan: a schedule of due dates,
    a dashboard of what's due today versus overdue, and a "Take Payment" flow that applies a
    payment across unpaid installments automatically, starting with the oldest due. Shops with
    pre-existing manual dues can bring them in as a starting balance rather than re-billing them.
  </p>

  <h2>Purchases &amp; suppliers</h2>
  <p>
    Record what you buy in from suppliers, and stock updates the same way it does on a sale —
    just in the other direction. Keep a simple list of suppliers instead of tracking purchases
    on paper or in a separate notebook.
  </p>

  <h2>Cash book</h2>
  <p>
    A running log of cash in and cash out — sales, payments received, and other cash movements —
    so the till balance is something you can check, not something you have to reconstruct at
    the end of the week.
  </p>

  <h2>Multi-outlet support</h2>
  <p>
    Running more than one shop? Add outlets under a single account, assign staff to a specific
    outlet, and see combined or per-outlet numbers in reports — without paying for or juggling a
    separate system per location.
  </p>

  <h2>Roles for your staff</h2>
  <p>
    Every staff member gets a role — <strong>Owner</strong>, <strong>Manager</strong>, or
    <strong>Cashier</strong> — with access scoped to what that role should see and do. A cashier
    can ring up sales without seeing margins or editing a closed day; a manager gets broader
    access without full ownership controls.
  </p>

  <h2>Repair jobs</h2>
  <p>
    For shops that also repair what they sell — phones, electronics — track a repair job from
    intake to handover: what came in, what's being done, and what the customer owes when it's
    picked up.
  </p>

  <h2>Corporate sales</h2>
  <p>
    Selling in bulk to a business or reseller account, alongside your regular walk-in customers?
    POS Plan keeps corporate/reseller sales distinct from everyday retail sales, without needing
    a separate system for it.
  </p>

  <h2>Multi-tenant, built to keep shops separate</h2>
  <p>
    POS Plan runs many shops on shared infrastructure, but each shop's data — customers,
    products, sales, staff — is isolated from every other shop on the platform. What you enter
    is yours to see; nothing crosses over between accounts.
  </p>

  <p><a href="https://app.erpboss.com/frontend/signup">Start your free trial</a> — no email needed.</p>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Base>
